            <ArticleTitle>[A periodontal furcation problem in a mandibular premolar].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>372-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>For several days a patient suffered from difficult to diagnose mandibular oral pain. The patient complained of pain and swelling for which no obvious explanation could be found. Eventually the cause became clear, as a second premolar with a mesial and distal root was found to have been affected by periodontal inflammation at the root furcation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
